>
>What about ya? That site lists their damage as the greatest of all
>projectiles, and they have a +1 to hit too.

  Arrows require wielding an appropriate launcher, otherwise they get a
-4 to-hit bonus.  Range is much more limited as well: just 6 at Str:25.
As opposed to range 12 for plain missiles.

  Compare the -4 to hit for an arrow thrown without wielding a launcher
with the intrinsic +2 for daggers, knives, and darts.

  Wielding a launcher is sufficiently complicating that I don't
recommend it.

  Arrows also vanish quickly.  At +0 an unblessed arrow has a 1/3 chance
of surviving a hit.   (Ditto for rocks, darts, crossbow bolts, etc.)
(A +2 non-blessed dart has a 50/50 chance of surviving two hits.)
(The way to keep arrows, darts, etc from vanishing is by blessing them
and maximizing luck.  High enchantment also helps.)

 Daggers and darts are no-hands weapons.  Daggers are multishot capable
and should always be #enhanced when possible.  Darts vanish too quickly
to be worth #enhancing.  Knives don't vanish but aren't multi-shot.
Don't enhance.




